// Input-parser fixture: every line ends with a space.
//
// §7.4 puts "surrounding horizontal space" on the caller, and `lines` is the
// caller. It implemented only half of that: `lines(int)` accepted " 1" and
// faulted on "1 ", while `grid(int)` over the identical bytes called the same
// run padding — two constructs disagreeing about one byte. The rule is
// `walk_exact`'s now, so every bounded construct inherits it.
//
// The last line also ends the file with a space before its newline, which is
// the ending no fixture in this directory had.
//
// Reference state: PASSES at the pre-S20 base b2184c8, fails at e68ac0c. A
// regression fixture for a defect this branch introduced and closed, not a gate
// for an audit finding.
var v = read lines(int)
out(v.len() * 10 + v.get(2))
